            "state": "",
            "type": "TextDisplay",
            "title": "Welcome to vSAN advanced network troubleshooting",
            "config": {
               "locationUrl": "",
               "locationFile": "",
               "editorData": "<font color=\"#ffffff\">Welcome to advanced vSAN network troubleshooting 201!\nAboove you will find 4 windows grouped by metric type.\nRDT latency tells you the latency of the vSAN transport protocol itself.\n\nTCP errors rolls up a few of the most common errors.\nbuffer overflow: likely increase your Pnic driver buffers\nCRC checksum mismatch: indicative of a upstream overrun and a tailstomp choping off the last of the packet.\nRX missed: typically buffer overflow, but this catches more. if buffer and this are equal, its a buffer increase to get rid of this.\n\n\nNetwork observations:\nThese are all counters showing whats happening on the network. duplicat acks are caused by latency and retransmission causing duplicate handshakes\nETC ETC<\/font>",
               "refreshInterval": 300,
               "widgetId": "d962c088-a1df-49cb-8cb1-8b7173cce9fc",
